# Reviewed and accepted findings, pinned by fingerprint.
#
# A fingerprint is commit:file:rule:line, so each entry exempts exactly one finding in one
# historical commit. A NEW secret in the same file, or the same value moving to another
# line, still fails the gate. That is why this file is used rather than a path exemption in
# .gitleaks.toml, which would blind the scanner to a whole directory forever.
#
# Every entry below was verified by decoding the value. None was ever a live credential,
# so nothing here needed rotating.
#
# Do not add to this file to make a build pass. If a finding is real, rotate the credential
# and rewrite the history that carries it.

